-- title:
--   Complementary principal ideals at a root of Φ_ℓ
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be a commutative integral domain and $B$ a commutative $A$-algebra, and let $\ell$ be a prime such that the image of $\ell$ in $A$ is a unit and such that $A$ contains a primitive $\ell$-th root of unity (that is, there exists $\omega \in A$ with `IsPrimitiveRoot ω ℓ`). Let $\xi \in B$ satisfy $\Phi_\ell(\xi) = 0$, where $\Phi_\ell$ is the $\ell$-th cyclotomic polynomial over $A$ and the evaluation is by the $A$-algebra map into $B$. Let $a \in A$ satisfy $a^{\ell} = 1$ and $a \neq 1$. The conclusion is that the two principal ideals of $B$ generated by $\xi - \mathrm{alg}(a)$ and by $\prod_{\mu} (\xi - \mathrm{alg}(\mu))$, the product being over the finset `primitiveRoots ℓ A` of primitive $\ell$-th roots of unity in $A$ with $a$ deleted (and $\mathrm{alg}$ denoting `algebraMap A B`), are complements in the lattice of ideals of $B$: their infimum is the zero ideal and their supremum is all of $B$.
--
--   This is the splitting step underlying the Chinese remainder decomposition of an $A$-algebra carrying a root of $\Phi_\ell$ into the factors cut out by the ideals $(\xi - a)$, one for each primitive $\ell$-th root of unity $a \in A$. It is used in the analysis of the components of a full-level modular curve construction, where it feeds the proof that the relevant quotient by such an ideal is a domain.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Ideal_isCompl_span_singleton_sub_algebraMap_of_aeval_cyclotomic_eq_zero.lean

